1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:10,840
Slide 11 presents our first major 실전 사례: CASE STUDY 1: 350-DESKTOP ENTERPRISE SEARCH: Eliminating File Chaos in a Global Accounting Firm.

2
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:20,242
Listen to this operational disaster, students: this accounting firm had 350 CPAs managing 4TB of tax filings on legacy Windows file servers.

3
00:00:20,242 --> 00:00:30,080
Every time a client called on the phone, the CPA had to click through 15 nested folders for 8 agonizing minutes just to find last year's 1040 tax return!

4
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:33,233
Eight minutes on every phone call!

5
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:38,660
That wasted 1,400 hours of high-billing CPA time every single week!

6
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:48,900
Management tried installing Google App for Windows, but it bogged down all their 8GB laptops and company compliance banned it because it sent file metadata to the public cloud!

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:58,717
Look at our Spark OS solution in Layer 2: we deployed a 35MB lightweight Rust/C++ local daemon tied to PowerToys Run.

8
00:00:58,717 --> 00:01:05,720
It indexed 2.4 million client tax PDFs into a local SQLite database in just 12 seconds!

9
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:13,336
Look at Layer 3: Now, when a client calls, the CPA taps `Alt + Space`, types the client's tax ID, and BAM!

10
00:01:13,336 --> 00:01:19,940
A full 5-year audit dossier pops up in 400 milliseconds—with ZERO data leaving the local network!

11
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:29,440
File retrieval time dropped by 99.2%, and the firm saved $180,000 in billable time in the very first quarter!

12
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:34,440
That is the power of lean, local-first architecture.

13
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:39,130
Now let us dissect the 1.2GB memory engine in Part 2!

